    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "> **R2 — split construction.** R2 is correct, and we thank them for the question. Our submitted split was random at the window level, so windows from the same student could appear in both train and test. We have re-split the data by student ID (StratifiedGroupKFold, 5 folds; the released test split contains no students seen in training) and re-run all models. Our best model's macro-F1 drops from 0.81 to 0.74, and the ranking of baselines is unchanged [verify]. We will (1) report both protocols in the paper to show the size of identity leakage in telemetry data, (2) make the student-grouped split the official benchmark split, and (3) add a datasheet note warning against window-level splits. All tables in the revision will use the grouped split.\n\nThat's 139 words. Check the \"[verify]\" claim before posting. If any baseline ranking changed, say so instead."
     ]
    },
